Z||000000||HYPTNOTiSE||05-29-2000||01:00 PM||||I just bought an 85 4 cyl 5 speed.  When it's wet the car runs really rough.  This thing has an edelbrock header on it, the oxygen sensor is in the collector, not sure if that might have anything to do with it.   The car acts like it's not getting enough gas, and it hesitates around 3K rpm.  At WOT this car gets up and goes!  What would happen if i just disconnect the 02 sensor temporarilly, would that just keep the car in open loop? Can an o2 sensor really make a car run rough? or might a tps also be the culprit although no other codes are showing up?<P>Mike LeCompte||||reg||8
Z||000001||theogre||05-30-2000||12:54 AM||||the haynes book says O2 sensor is bitching.<P>the relocated O2 sensor may be part of it. Is the O2 new? If not put in a new Bosch unit. (I never buy anything but Bosch O2 sensors. Bosch invented these and still makes the best ones.)<P>you indicate it's more prevalent when wet. Haynes also says check TPS. I'd definatly replace that. A worn TPS will let in water which will screw up it's readings.||||reg||1
